--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusConn
is: ^conn
icon: "modbus"
connFeatures: {learn, pollMode:"buckets"}
doc: "Modbus connector"
linter: "modbusExt::LintModbus"
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
defx: ^uri
tagOn: ^modbusConn
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Tags
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusBlockGap
is: ^int
tagOn: ^modbusConn
doc:
  Applied to 'modbusConn' to allow for gaps in block reads. See
  `ext-modbus::doc#blockReads` for more information.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusBlockMax
is: ^int
tagOn: ^modbusConn
doc:
  Applied to 'modbusConn' to limit the maximum number of registers to read in a
  block read. See `ext-modbus::doc#blockReads` for more information.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusFrameDelay
is: ^duration
tagOn: [^modbusConn, ^connTuning]
doc:
  Minimum silence to enforce on the wire between two consecutive transactions.
  Applied to 'modbusConn' or its 'connTuning' rec. A value on the conn rec takes
  precedence. Defaults to 0sec.

  All conns sharing a 'uri' share one connection, and their requests are issued
  back-to-back with no gap. A multi-drop TCP-to-RTU gateway needs turnaround time
  to switch bus direction and to give the slaves their 3.5 char-time silence;
  without it the second request in a burst is dropped on the serial side with no
  exception response, which surfaces as a read timeout. Set this to 50ms or more
  when several slaves share a gateway.

  Note this delay is inside the window bounded by `modbusReadTimeout` and
  `modbusWriteTimeout`, so those must be large enough to cover the whole
  serialized cycle for every slave on the uri. See `ext-modbus::doc#frameDelay`
  for more information.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusRegMapUri
is: ^uri
tagOn: ^modbusConn
uiInput: "modbusExt::ModbusRegMapInput"
doc:
  Applied to 'modbusConn' to define the register map CSV file.
  This URI must be a path relative to the project's home directory
  or can be a "fan://" URI to a CSV file bundled in a pod.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusSlave
is: ^int
tagOn: ^modbusConn
doc:
  Applied to 'modbusConn' to identify the slave address on this
  modbus network.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusReadTimeout
is: ^duration
tagOn: ^modbusConn
doc:
  How long to wait before timing out on a modbus read.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
def: ^modbusWriteTimeout
is: ^duration
tagOn: ^modbusConn
doc:
  How long to wait before timing out on a modbus write.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
